Typing in the search box no longer hangs the page
==================================================

The tools page has a search that filters connections and skill cards, and an observer on the document so
the filter survives the lists being redrawn. The filter also WRITES to the document: it sets `hidden` on
every card and replaces the count's text on every pass.

`status.textContent = …` fires the observer, the observer calls the filter, the filter writes the count
again — a loop with no exit that keeps the renderer busy for as long as the page is open. It only shows
up when the box is used, which is why the page looked fine: one character typed into it wedged the
window, and the automation bridge answered `action_timeout` because the webview never came back.

Both writes are conditional now. `status.textContent` is only assigned when the text differs, and
`hidden` only when the value changes, so the observer settles after one pass instead of re-firing on its
own output.

---
--- a/resources/ui/capability-workflows.js
+++ b/resources/ui/capability-workflows.js
@@ -263,6 +263,11 @@
         "aria-label": "Search connections, tools and skills",
       });
       const status = el("p", { class: "hint", role: "status" });
+      // Every write here is conditional, and that is not cosmetic. This function is called by the
+      // observer below on any DOM change, and it also CHANGES the DOM — so an unconditional
+      // `status.textContent = …` re-fires the observer on its own write and the page spins forever.
+      // Typing one character in this box hung the window: the eval bridge timed out while the renderer
+      // was still looping. Same for `node.hidden`, which is an attribute write on every card.
       const apply = () => {
         const needle = input.value.trim().toLocaleLowerCase();
         let shown = 0;
@@ -270,10 +275,11 @@
         for (const node of document.querySelectorAll("#mcp-connections [data-server], .cards .skill-card")) {
           total += 1;
           const hit = !needle || node.textContent.toLocaleLowerCase().includes(needle);
-          node.hidden = !hit;
+          if (node.hidden === hit) node.hidden = !hit;
           if (hit) shown += 1;
         }
-        status.textContent = needle ? `${shown} of ${total} match "${input.value.trim()}"` : "";
+        const text = needle ? `${shown} of ${total} match "${input.value.trim()}"` : "";
+        if (status.textContent !== text) status.textContent = text;
       };
       input.addEventListener("input", apply);
       // both lists are drawn after this renders, so re-apply when the DOM changes
